#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/openssh.xml:116
#, xml-text
msgid "Installation of OpenSSH"
msgstr "Instalação do OpenSSH"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/openssh.xml:119
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<application>OpenSSH</application> runs as two processes when connecting to "
"other computers. The first process is a privileged process and controls the "
"issuance of privileges as necessary. The second process communicates with "
"the network. Additional installation steps are necessary to set up the "
"proper environment, which are performed by issuing the following commands as"
" the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""
"O <application>OpenSSH</application> executa como dois processos ao se "
"conectar a outros computadores. O primeiro processo é um processo "
"privilegiado e controla a emissão de privilégios conforme necessário. O "
"segundo processo se comunica com a rede de intercomunicação. Etapas "
"adicionais de instalação são necessárias para configurar o ambiente "
"adequado, que são realizadas emitindo os seguintes comandos como o(a) "
"usuário(a) <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem>:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/openssh.xml:127
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>install -v -g sys -m700 -d /var/lib/sshd &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"groupadd -g 50 sshd        &amp;&amp;\n"
"useradd  -c 'sshd PrivSep' \\\n"
"         -d /var/lib/sshd  \\\n"
"         -g sshd           \\\n"
"         -s /bin/false     \\\n"
"         -u 50 sshd</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>install -v -g sys -m700 -d /var/lib/sshd &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"groupadd -g 50 sshd        &amp;&amp;\n"
"useradd  -c 'sshd PrivSep' \\\n"
"         -d /var/lib/sshd  \\\n"
"         -g sshd           \\\n"
"         -s /bin/false     \\\n"
"         -u 50 sshd</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/openssh.xml:164
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Install <application>OpenSSH</application> by running the following "
"commands:"
msgstr ""
"Instale o <application>OpenSSH</application> executando os seguintes "
"comandos:"

#.  -\-with-md5-passwords used to be here, but a comment inside of a <screen>
#.      block leaves an eyesore.
#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/openssh.xml:170
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>./configure --prefix=/usr                            \\\n"
"            --sysconfdir=/etc/ssh                    \\\n"
"            --with-privsep-path=/var/lib/sshd        \\\n"
"            --with-default-path=/usr/bin             \\\n"
"            --with-superuser-path=/usr/sbin:/usr/bin \\\n"
"            --with-pid-dir=/run                      &amp;&amp;\n"
"make</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>./configure --prefix=/usr                           \\\n"
"            --sysconfdir=/etc/ssh                    \\\n"
"            --with-privsep-path=/var/lib/sshd        \\\n"
"            --with-default-path=/usr/bin             \\\n"
"            --with-superuser-path=/usr/sbin:/usr/bin \\\n"
"            --with-pid-dir=/run                      &amp;&amp;\n"
"make</userinput>"

#. One test, <filename>
#. key options</filename>, fails when run in chroot.
#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/openssh.xml:196
#, xml-text
msgid "To test the results, issue: <command>make -j1 tests</command>."
msgstr "Para testar os resultados, emita: <command>make -j1 tests</command>."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/openssh.xml:219
#, xml-text
msgid "Now, as the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""
"Agora, como o(a) usuário(a) <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem>:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/openssh.xml:222
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>make install &amp;&amp;\n"
"install -v -m755    contrib/ssh-copy-id /usr/bin     &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"install -v -m644    contrib/ssh-copy-id.1 \\\n"
"                    /usr/share/man/man1              &amp;&amp;\n"
"install -v -m755 -d /usr/share/doc/openssh-&openssh-version;     &amp;&amp;\n"
"install -v -m644    INSTALL LICENCE OVERVIEW README* \\\n"
"                    /usr/share/doc/openssh-&openssh-version;</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>make install &amp;&amp;\n"
"install -v -m755   contrib/ssh-copy-id /usr/bin     &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"install -v -m644    contrib/ssh-copy-id.1 \\\n"
"                    /usr/share/man/man1              &amp;&amp;\n"
"install -v -m755 -d /usr/share/doc/openssh-&openssh-version;     &amp;&amp;\n"
"install -v -m644    INSTALL LICENCE OVERVIEW README* \\\n"
"                    /usr/share/doc/openssh-&openssh-version;</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/openssh.xml:233
#, xml-text
msgid "Command Explanations"
msgstr "Explicações do Comando"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/openssh.xml:236
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>--sysconfdir=/etc/ssh</parameter>: This prevents the "
"configuration files from being installed in <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/usr/etc</filename>."
msgstr ""
"<parameter>--sysconfdir=/etc/ssh</parameter>: Isso evita que os arquivos de "
"configuração sejam instalados em <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/usr/etc</filename>."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/openssh.xml:242
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>--with-default-path=/usr/bin</parameter> and <parameter>--with-"
"superuser-path=/usr/sbin:/usr/bin</parameter>: These set the "
"<envar>PATH</envar> setting to be consistent with the LFS and BLFS "
"<application>Shadow</application> package."
msgstr ""
"<parameter>--with-default-path=/usr/bin</parameter> e <parameter>--with-"
"superuser-path=/usr/sbin:/usr/bin</parameter>: Esses configuram a "
"configuração de <envar>PATH</envar> para estar consistente com o pacote "
"<application>Shadow</application> do LFS e do BLFS."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/openssh.xml:249
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>--with-pid-dir=/run</parameter>: This prevents "
"<application>OpenSSH</application> from referring to the deprecated "
"<filename class=\"directory\">/var/run</filename> directory."
msgstr ""
"<parameter>--with-pid-dir=/run</parameter>: Isso evita que "
"<application>OpenSSH</application> se refira ao diretório obsoleto <filename"
" class=\"directory\">/var/run</filename>."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/openssh.xml:264
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<option>--with-pam</option>: This option enables <application>Linux-"
"PAM</application> support in the build. If you use this option, ensure that "
"you create the PAM configuration in the Configuration Information section "
"below."
msgstr ""
"<option>--with-pam</option>: Essa opção habilita o suporte "
"<application>Linux-PAM</application> na construção. Se você usar essa opção,"
" assegure-se de criar a configuração do PAM na seção Informações de "
"Configuração abaixo."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/openssh.xml:271
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<option>--with-xauth=$XORG_PREFIX/bin/xauth</option>: This sets the default "
"location for the <command>xauth</command> binary for X authentication. The "
"environment variable <envar>XORG_PREFIX</envar> should be set following "
"<xref linkend='xorg-env'/>. This can also be controlled from "
"<filename>sshd_config</filename> with the XAuthLocation keyword. You can "
"omit this switch if <command>xauth</command> (one of <xref "
"linkend=\"xorg7-app\"/>) is already installed."
msgstr ""
"<option>--with-xauth=$XORG_PREFIX/bin/xauth</option>: Isso configura o local"
" padrão para o binário <command>xauth</command> para autenticação do X. A "
"variável de ambiente <envar>XORG_PREFIX</envar> deveria estar configurada "
"seguindo-se <xref linkend='xorg-env'/>. Isso também pode ser controlado a "
"partir de <filename>sshd_config</filename> com a palavra-chave "
"XAuthLocation. Você pode omitir essa chave se o <command>xauth</command> (um"
" dos <xref linkend=\"xorg7-app\"/>) já estiver instalado."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/openssh.xml:281
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<option>--with-kerberos5=/usr</option>: This option is used to include "
"Kerberos 5 support in the build."
msgstr ""
"<option>--with-kerberos5=/usr</option>: Essa opção é usada para incluir "
"suporte a Kerberos 5 na construção."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/openssh.xml:286
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<option>--with-libedit</option>: This option enables line editing and "
"history features for <command>sftp</command>."
msgstr ""
"<option>--with-libedit</option>: Essa opção habilita a edição de linha e "
"recursos de histórico para o <command>sftp</command>."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/openssh.xml:293
#, xml-text
msgid "Configuring OpenSSH"
msgstr "Configurando o OpenSSH"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/openssh.xml:296
#, xml-text
msgid "Config Files"
msgstr "Arquivos de Configuração"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/openssh.xml:299
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<filename>~/.ssh/*</filename>, <filename>/etc/ssh/ssh_config</filename>, and"
" <filename>/etc/ssh/sshd_config</filename>"
msgstr ""
"<filename>~/.ssh/*</filename>, <filename>/etc/ssh/ssh_config</filename> e "
"<filename>/etc/ssh/sshd_config</filename>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><indexterm><primary>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/openssh.xml:305
#, xml-text
msgid "~/.ssh/*"
msgstr "~/.ssh/*"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><indexterm><primary>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/openssh.xml:309
#, xml-text
msgid "/etc/ssh/ssh_config"
msgstr "/etc/ssh/ssh_config"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><indexterm><primary>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/openssh.xml:313
#, xml-text
msgid "/etc/ssh/sshd_config"
msgstr "/etc/ssh/sshd_config"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/openssh.xml:317
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"There are no required changes to any of these files. However, you may wish "
"to view the <filename class='directory'>/etc/ssh/</filename> files and make "
"any changes appropriate for the security of your system. One recommended "
"change is that you disable <systemitem class='username'>root</systemitem> "
"login via <command>ssh</command>. Execute the following command as the "
"<systemitem class='username'>root</systemitem> user to disable <systemitem "
"class='username'>root</systemitem> login via <command>ssh</command>:"
msgstr ""
"Não existem mudanças exigidas para nenhum desses arquivos. No entanto, você "
"possivelmente deseje visualizar os arquivos do <filename "
"class='directory'>/etc/ssh/</filename> e fazer quaisquer mudanças "
"apropriadas para a segurança do teu sistema. Uma mudança recomendada é a de "
"desabilitar o login do(a) <systemitem class='username'>root</systemitem> via"
" <command>ssh</command>. Execute o seguinte comando como o(a) usuário(a) "
"<systemitem class='username'>root</systemitem> para desabilitar o login "
"do(a) <systemitem class='username'>root</systemitem> via "
"<command>ssh</command>:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/openssh.xml:329
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>echo \"PermitRootLogin no\" &gt;&gt; "
"/etc/ssh/sshd_config</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>echo \"PermitRootLogin no\" &gt;&gt; "
"/etc/ssh/sshd_config</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/openssh.xml:332
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you want to be able to log in without typing in your password, first "
"create ~/.ssh/id_rsa and ~/.ssh/id_rsa.pub with <command>ssh-"
"keygen</command> and then copy ~/.ssh/id_rsa.pub to ~/.ssh/authorized_keys "
"on the remote computer that you want to log into.  You'll need to change "
"REMOTE_USERNAME and REMOTE_HOSTNAME for the username and hostname of the "
"remote computer and you'll also need to enter your password for the ssh-"
"copy-id command to succeed:"
msgstr ""
"Se quiser estar apto(a) a se logar sem digitar tua senha, crie primeiro "
"~/.ssh/id_rsa e ~/.ssh/id_rsa.pub com o <command>ssh-keygen</command> e "
"depois copie ~/.ssh /id_rsa.pub para ~/.ssh/authorized_keys no computador "
"remoto no qual deseja se logar. Você precisará mudar NOME_USUARIO(A)_REMOTO "
"e NOME_DISPOSITIVO_REMOTO para o nome de usuário(a) e nome do dispositivo do"
" computador remoto e também precisará inserir tua senha para que o comando "
"ssh-copy-id seja bem-sucedido:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/openssh.xml:341
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>ssh-keygen &amp;&amp;\n"
"ssh-copy-id -i ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub <replaceable>REMOTE_USERNAME</replaceable>@<replaceable>REMOTE_HOSTNAME</replaceable></userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>ssh-keygen &amp;&amp;\n"
"ssh-copy-id -i ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub <replaceable>NOME_USUÁRIO(A)_REMOTO</replaceable>@<replaceable>NOME_DISPOSITIVO_REMOTO</replaceable></userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/openssh.xml:345
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Once you've got passwordless logins working it's actually more secure than "
"logging in with a password (as the private key is much longer than most "
"people's passwords). If you would like to now disable password logins, as "
"the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""
"Tão logo tenha obtido logins sem senha funcionando, atualmente é mais seguro"
" que se logar com uma senha (já que a chave privada é muito mais longa que "
"as senhas da maioria das pessoas). Se você gostaria de desabilitar logins de"
" senha agora, como o(a) usuário(a) <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem>:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/openssh.xml:352
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>echo \"PasswordAuthentication no\" >> /etc/ssh/sshd_config &amp;&amp;\n"
"echo \"KbdInteractiveAuthentication no\" >> /etc/ssh/sshd_config</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>echo \"PasswordAuthentication no\" >> /etc/ssh/sshd_config &amp;&amp;\n"
"echo \"KbdInteractiveAuthentication no\" >> /etc/ssh/sshd_config</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/openssh.xml:356
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you added <application>Linux-PAM</application> support and you want ssh "
"to use it then you will need to add a configuration file for "
"<application>sshd</application> and enable use of "
"<application>LinuxPAM</application>. Note, ssh only uses PAM to check "
"passwords, if you've disabled password logins these commands are not needed."
" If you want to use PAM, issue the following commands as the <systemitem "
"class='username'>root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""
"Se você adicionou suporte <application>Linux-PAM</application> e deseja que "
"o ssh o use, então precisará adicionar um arquivo de configuração para o "
"<application>sshd</application> e habilitar o uso do <application>Linux-"
"PAM</application>. Observe que o ssh somente usa PAM para verificar senhas; "
"se tiver desabilitado os logins de senha, estes comandos não são "
"necessários. Se você deseja usar o PAM, emita os seguintes comandos como "
"o(a) usuário(a) <systemitem class='username'>root</systemitem>:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/openssh.xml:365
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>sed 's@d/login@d/sshd@g' /etc/pam.d/login &gt; /etc/pam.d/sshd &amp;&amp;\n"
"chmod 644 /etc/pam.d/sshd &amp;&amp;\n"
"echo \"UsePAM yes\" &gt;&gt; /etc/ssh/sshd_config</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>sed 's@d/login@d/sshd@g' /etc/pam.d/login &gt; /etc/pam.d/sshd &amp;&amp;\n"
"chmod 644 /etc/pam.d/sshd &amp;&amp;\n"
"echo \"UsePAM yes\" &gt;&gt; /etc/ssh/sshd_config</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/openssh.xml:370
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Additional configuration information can be found in the man pages for "
"<command>sshd</command>, <command>ssh</command> and <command>ssh-"
"agent</command>."
msgstr ""
"Informação adicional de configuração pode ser encontrada nas páginas de "
"manual para <command>sshd</command>, <command>ssh</command> e <command>ssh-"
